{"title":"Career Roadmap · Paper Technologist","role":"Paper Technologist","summary":"A Paper Technologist works on the science, engineering, manufacturing, testing and improvement of paper, paperboard, specialty papers and coated paper products.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Pulp, Paper & Coating Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Paper Technologist works on the science, engineering, manufacturing, testing and improvement of paper, paperboard, specialty papers and coated paper products."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines pulp and fiber science, chemistry, materials engineering, process engineering, paper-machine operations, coating technology, quality control and process optimization."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong modern Paper Technologist should understand not only conventional papermaking but also recycled fibers, sustainable materials, barrier coatings, specialty papers, automation, process analytics and energy-efficient manufacturing."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Career Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Pulp & Fiber Science","Paper Manufacturing","Coating Technology","Materials Science","Process Control","Quality","Sustainability","Data Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E. Pulp, Paper & Coating Technology","Pulp & Fiber Science Fundamentals","Paper Chemistry & Material Properties","Pulping → Bleaching → Stock Preparation","Papermaking & Paper Machine Systems","Drying → Calendaring → Finishing","Coating Technology & Surface Treatment","Testing + Quality Control + Optimization","Automation + Process Data + Sustainability","Industrial Internship","Paper Technologist Trainee","Paper Technologist","Senior Paper / Process Technologist","R&D / Process Development / Production Specialist","Technical Manager / Plant Specialist"]}]},{"heading":"C